Code adapted from xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
And also very messy

You have to download libdrmtap from https://github.com/fxd0h/libdrmtap and modify make.sh (sorry dont have proper makefile yet)
give the xdg-desktop-portal-x11-session program admin caps (so it can grab the output of the GPU through drmtap)
using:
# setcap cap_sys_admin+ep xdg-desktop-portal-x11-session

To make sure programs can talk to the portal using dbus it will have to be registered in the xdg-desktop portal

Files setup for portal (might differ on distro idk, this is for arch):
put x11-portals.conf in /usr/share/xdg-desktop-portal/
put x11.portal in /usr/share/xdg-desktop-portal/portals/
put org.freedesktop.impl.portal.desktop.x11.service in /usr/share/dbus-1/services/
put xdg-desktop-portal-x11.service in /usr/lib/systemd/user/
put xdg-desktop-portal-x11 & xdg-desktop-portal-x11-session in /lib/

after that (hopefully to portal files i made work outside i3)
systemctl --user restart xdg-desktop-portal
then run the portal manually (doesnt yet work if started by xdg-desktop-portal)
./xdg-desktop-portal-x11
and then you get log

open OBS or wayvr and it should work

